1
00:00:00,700 --> 00:00:02,694
An air conditioner does not make cold air.

2
00:00:03,224 --> 00:00:04,905
It moves heat.

3
00:00:05,435 --> 00:00:07,828
It picks up heat inside your room,

4
00:00:08,058 --> 00:00:09,701
and carries it outside.

5
00:00:10,581 --> 00:00:13,748
The secret is a fluid called a refrigerant.

6
00:00:14,278 --> 00:00:17,167
When a liquid evaporates, it absorbs heat.

7
00:00:17,697 --> 00:00:20,770
When a vapor condenses, it releases heat.

8
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,322
An air conditioner uses both,

9
00:00:23,552 --> 00:00:25,379
in a closed loop.

10
00:00:26,259 --> 00:00:28,763
Step one: the compressor.

11
00:00:29,293 --> 00:00:32,548
It squeezes low-pressure refrigerant vapor

12
00:00:33,078 --> 00:00:35,571
into a hot, high-pressure gas.

13
00:00:36,451 --> 00:00:40,038
Step two: the condenser, in the outdoor unit.

14
00:00:40,568 --> 00:00:43,832
A fan blows outside air across the hot coil.

15
00:00:44,362 --> 00:00:46,178
The gas releases its heat,

16
00:00:46,408 --> 00:00:49,346
and condenses into a high-pressure liquid.

17
00:00:50,226 --> 00:00:53,018
Step three: the expansion valve.

18
00:00:53,548 --> 00:00:55,862
The liquid is forced through a narrow opening.

19
00:00:56,392 --> 00:00:58,644
Its pressure drops suddenly,

20
00:00:58,874 --> 00:01:01,070
and it becomes very cold.

21
00:01:01,950 --> 00:01:05,814
Step four: the evaporator, in the indoor unit.

22
00:01:06,344 --> 00:01:09,826
A fan pulls warm room air across the cold coil.

23
00:01:10,356 --> 00:01:13,552
The refrigerant absorbs the heat and evaporates.

24
00:01:14,082 --> 00:01:16,427
The air comes out cooler.

25
00:01:17,307 --> 00:01:19,055
The vapor returns to the compressor,

26
00:01:19,285 --> 00:01:20,988
and the cycle repeats.

27
00:01:21,518 --> 00:01:26,519
Compress, condense, expand, evaporate.

28
00:01:27,049 --> 00:01:29,243
Heat in from your room,

29
00:01:29,473 --> 00:01:30,944
heat out to the outdoors.
